Linking complications to specific MD groups
Normalizing readmission rates across DRGs
Adjusting for expected benchmarks in Tableau

Patient Demographics & Equity Dashboard 3
> Software Used
Designed in Tableau, leveraging its strength in categorical filtering and equity-focused breakdowns.
> Intended Audience
Health equity analysts, public health agencies, and hospital DEI (diversity, equity, inclusion) teams.
> Message Conveyed
Displays disparities in self-reported health ratings across sex, language spoken at home, region, and education level—revealing potential access and outcome inequities.
> Design Considerations
Stacked Bars: Present gradations in health perception clearly
Segmented Views: Organized by language, geography, and education for easy comparison
Color Palette: Shades from yellow to dark green denote health rating levels
> Reproducibility
Filterable by multiple variables. Tableau’s logic and structure can be saved for repeated analysis with new data inputs.
> Accessibility
Good use of visual segmentation and consistent legends. Still, Tableau lacks built-in screen reader compatibility—text alternatives should be exported.
> Impacted Communities
Racialized and multilingual populations, undereducated groups, and residents in lower-income Toronto regions.
> Feature Selection
Prioritized categories aligned with social determinants of health (language, region, education). Excluded income and immigration status for privacy or data completeness concerns.
> Underwater Labour
Recoding education and language from intake forms
Aligning demographic data to standard census regions
Cleaning self-reported health data into unified categories

